<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ADDED 17 Oct 2026 - the filled arc of a countdown ring, depleting as the
     deadline approaches.

     The colour here is the arc's ONLY colour. An earlier version of this file
     said the provider overrides it per-push with setProgressTintList() so the
     arc could carry the urgency (good -> warn -> urgent) - and that is NOT
     POSSIBLE: RemoteViews.setProgressTintList is a @hide API missing from the
     SDK level this project compiles against, and build-apk rejected every
     call site with "cannot find symbol". So the arc stays widget_good in
     every state, and the urgency signal is the status WORD beside it, which
     setTextColor can still recolour. Pinned by widgetRingGuard.

     android:useLevel="true" HERE, and "false" on the track - the two layers
     need opposite attributes, and the reason is in widget_ring_track.xml's
     own comment: setProgressBar moves this layer's sweep by setting its
     level, and a shape that ignores the level would draw a full circle no
     matter what progress says.

     Geometry MUST match widget_ring_track.xml exactly - innerRadius 16dp +
     thickness 6dp, a 44dp ring whose hole is 32dp - because a mismatch draws
     two concentric rings of different diameters rather than one arc over one
     track. Both were changed together on 20 Oct 2026, when the ring shrank
     from 52dp: a 52dp ring inside a 44dp view is CLIPPED, not scaled, so
     leaving the drawable alone would have cut the ring's edge off. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="ring"
    android:innerRadius="16dp"
    android:thickness="6dp"
    android:useLevel="true">
    <solid android:color="@color/widget_good" />
</shape>
